---
import { lines, products } from './facts.mjs';
---
<figure class="repair" data-repair aria-label="Moving each fact to its own table">
  <figcaption><span>Figure 4</span> Moving each fact to its own table</figcaption>
  <div class="scene" data-live>
    <section data-scene="0">
      <h4>One table · one row per order line</h4>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Flattened order lines"><table><thead><tr><th>Order / line</th><th>Placed (UTC)</th><th>Customer</th><th>Product</th><th>Qty</th><th>Agreed</th></tr></thead><tbody>{lines.map(l=><tr><td>{l.order} / {l.line}</td><td>{l.order===101?'12 Oct 09:30':'20 Oct 10:15'}</td><td>1 · Mina Shah</td><td>{l.product} · {products.find(p=>p.id===l.product)?.name}</td><td>{l.quantity}</td><td>{l.price}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="notice">The same order date and customer name occur once per line.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-scene="1" hidden>
      <h4>Move order facts out of the lines</h4>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Orders separated from order lines"><table><caption>orders · one row per order</caption><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Placed (UTC)</th><th>Customer</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>12 Oct 09:30</td><td>1 · Mina Shah</td></tr><tr><td>103</td><td>20 Oct 10:15</td><td>1 · Mina Shah</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Order lines after separating order facts"><table><caption>order_items · one row per line</caption><thead><tr><th>Order / line</th><th>Product</th><th>Qty</th><th>Agreed</th></tr></thead><tbody>{lines.map(l=><tr><td>{l.order} / {l.line}</td><td>{l.product} · {products.find(p=>p.id===l.product)?.name}</td><td>{l.quantity}</td><td>{l.price}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
      <p class="notice">The date now occurs once per order. Mina’s name still occurs once per order.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-scene="2" hidden>
      <h4>Move customer and product facts out too</h4>
      <div class="homes"><div><b>customers</b><p>1 · Mina Shah</p></div><div><b>products</b>{products.map(p=><p>{p.id} · {p.name}</p>)}</div></div>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Orders referencing the customer"><table><caption>orders</caption><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Placed (UTC)</th><th>Customer ID</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>101</td><td>12 Oct 09:30</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>103</td><td>20 Oct 10:15</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <div class="region" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Lines referencing products"><table><caption>order_items</caption><thead><tr><th>Order / line</th><th>Product ID</th><th>Qty</th><th>Agreed</th></tr></thead><tbody>{lines.map(l=><tr><td>{l.order} / {l.line}</td><td>{l.product}</td><td>{l.quantity}</td><td>{l.price}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
    </section>
    <section data-scene="3" hidden>
      <h4>Correct the current customer name in one place</h4>
      <div class="homes"><div><b>customers</b><p>1 · Mina Shah<br/>↓<br/><strong>1 · Meena Shah</strong></p></div><div><b>orders</b><p>101 → customer 1</p><p>103 → customer 1</p></div></div>
      <p class="notice">Both orders still identify the same customer. Neither order row needs a name correction.</p>
    </section>
    <p data-explanation aria-live="polite">Start with four lines. The date belongs to the order; the current customer name belongs to customer 1.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Controls for figure 4">
    <button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span>
    <div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="scroll-hint">Scroll wide tables sideways to see every column.</p>
  <p class="caption">A conceptual repair of the shop data, with selected columns. All dates are in October 2026. Each table keeps the identifier needed to recover its associations.</p>
  <details><summary>All four stages, as text</summary><ol><li>The flattened table repeats an order’s date on each line, and the customer’s current name on each of that customer’s lines.</li><li>Separating orders removes repeated dates from the lines. Customer names still repeat across orders.</li><li>Customers hold current names; products hold catalogue names. Orders reference customers and lines reference products. The agreed price stays on the line.</li><li>A hypothetical correction from Mina to Meena changes customer 1 once. Orders 101 and 103 still reference customer 1.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for (const root of document.querySelectorAll('[data-repair]')) {
  const explanations = [
    'Start with four lines. The date belongs to the order; the current customer name belongs to customer 1.',
    'The order date now has one home per order. Mina’s name still repeats because it belongs to the customer, not to each order.',
    'Each current name now has one home. Repeated IDs keep the associations; the line still holds its own quantity and agreed price.',
    'Correct the current name once. Reading either order through customer 1 now gives Meena Shah. This is an illustrative correction, not a change to the shop’s starting facts.'
  ];
  stepper(root, {steps:()=>4, draw: step => {
    for (const panel of root.querySelectorAll('[data-scene]')) panel.hidden = Number(panel.dataset.scene) !== step;
    root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent = explanations[step];
  }});
}
</script>
<style>
.repair { margin:2.5rem 0; font-family:var(--font-sans); }
figcaption { font:500 1.06rem/1.5 var(--font-serif); margin-bottom:.75rem; }
figcaption span { font:.67rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.1em; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin-right:.7rem; }
.scene { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:1rem; background:var(--color-surface); font:.82rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
.scene > section {margin:0;}
.scroll-hint {display:none;}
h4 { margin:0 0 .8rem; font:500 .92rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
.region {overflow-x:auto; margin:.8rem 0;}
.region:focus-visible {outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px;}
table {display:table;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:0;font:inherit;}
th,td {padding:.5rem;text-align:left;white-space:nowrap;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);}
caption {text-align:left;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-bottom:.3rem;}
p {font:inherit;}
.notice {margin:1rem 0;color:var(--color-text-secondary);}
[data-explanation] {margin:1rem 0 0;border-left:3px solid var(--teal);padding:.7rem .8rem;}
.homes {display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr;gap:.8rem;}
.homes > div {padding:.7rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);}
.homes p {margin:.5rem 0;}
.controls {display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-top:0;background:var(--color-surface-alt);font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);}
button {font:inherit;padding:.5rem .7rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:4px;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);cursor:pointer;}
button:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible {outline:2px solid var(--teal);outline-offset:3px;}
button[aria-disabled="true"] {color:var(--color-text-secondary);cursor:default;}
[data-hold] {width:100%;height:3px;background:var(--color-rule);}
[data-hold] span {display:block;width:0;height:100%;background:var(--teal);}
.caption,details {font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary);}
summary {cursor:pointer;text-decoration:underline;}
[hidden] {display:none;}
@media(max-width:550px) {.scroll-hint {display:block;font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text-secondary);} .homes {grid-template-columns:1fr;} .scene {padding:.8rem;} }
</style>
